-- title:
--   Elliptic twisted terms assemble into the base-change elliptic sum
-- statement:
--   Setting. $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ a finite Galois extension whose degree $\ell := [L:K]$, i.e. `Module.finrank K L`, is prime (`hprime`); $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ satisfies $\sigma \neq 1$ (`hσ`) and `hgen` requires every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to lie in the cyclic subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (`σ.symm`). Two reals $\alpha,\beta$ are given with $0 < \alpha$ and $\alpha < \beta$. The idele groups $(\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$ and $(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$ carry Borel measurable structures and Haar measures $\nu_{Z,L}$ and $\nu_{Z,K}$. The datum $D$ is an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 L) K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28), that is, a homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K) \to \mathrm{RingAut}(\mathbb{A}_L)$ which is continuous in each element and compatible with the embedding of $L$; $\sigma^{-1}$ acts on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ entrywise through $D$, written [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14). Throughout, `globalPoints` is the entrywise map $\mathrm{GL}_2(F) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, `centralScalar` is the scalar embedding $(\mathbb{A}_F)^{\times} \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, `ideleNorm` is the modulus character given by the distributive Haar character, and $N$ denotes the idelic norm $(\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$ attached to the base change [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87) (the unit map of the algebra norm).
--
--   Characters. $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top \le (\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$ to $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ whose associated complex-valued function is continuous (`hξc`) and which is trivial on the principal ideles, i.e. on the range of $L^{\times} \to (\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$ (`hξt`). $\Xi$ is a finite set of homomorphisms $\top \le (\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times} \to \mathbb{C}^{\times}$, and `hΞ` characterises membership: $\xi \in \Xi$ if and only if $\xi$ is continuous as a complex-valued function, trivial on the principal ideles of $K$, and satisfies $\xi \circ N = \xi_L$.
--
--   Twisted classes over $L$. $R_L \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ is contained (`hRLsub`) in the set of those $\delta$ for which the norm class $\mathrm{normClassMap}_{hgen}$ of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class of $\delta$ equals the conjugacy class of some $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ lying in the elliptic cell (the characteristic polynomial of $\gamma$ has no root in $K$) or in the central cell ($\gamma$ is a scalar matrix); and `hRL` requires that every $\delta$ of that set admit a unique $\delta_0 \in R_L$ together with $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $u \in L^{\times}$ with $\delta = u \cdot (h^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(h))$, the scalar $u$ acting as a central element. For each $\delta_0 \in R_L$ the set $\Psi_L(\delta_0) \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ lies in the slab $\{g : \mathrm{ideleNorm}_L(\det g) \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΨLs`) and is a fundamental domain (`hΨL`) for the image under `globalPoints` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) : t\,\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1} = \delta_0\}$, with respect to the adelic Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ restricted to that slab. The set $\Theta \subseteq (\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$ is a fundamental domain, for $\nu_{Z,L}$, of the image in $(\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$ of the subgroup $\{\sigma^{-1}(u)u^{-1} : u \in L^{\times}\}$ of $L^{\times}$ (`hΘ`).
--
--   Classes over $K$. $R_K \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ is contained in the union of the central and elliptic cells (`hRKsub`), and `hRK` requires that every $\gamma$ in that union admit a unique $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ with $\gamma = a \cdot (h^{-1}\gamma_0 h)$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ and some central scalar $a \in K^{\times}$. For $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ the set $\Psi_K(\gamma_0) \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ lies in the slab $\{g : \mathrm{ideleNorm}_K(\det g) \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΨKs`) and is a fundamental domain (`hΨK`) for the image under `globalPoints` of the centraliser of $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, with respect to `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ restricted to that slab.
--
--   Constants and measure comparison. $c_0$ is a non-negative real constant and $\kappa > 0$ (`hκ`). The hypothesis `hκl` states that for every measurable $g : (\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times} \to [0,\infty]$ one has $\int^{-}_{\Theta} g(N z)\,d\nu_{Z,L} = \kappa \cdot \int^{-}_{\mathrm{range}\,N} g\,d\nu_{Z,K}$ as lower Lebesgue integrals, and `hκi` states that for every measurable $g : (\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times} \to \mathbb{C}$ the function $z \mapsto g(Nz)$ is integrable on $\Theta$ for $\nu_{Z,L}$ if and only if $g$ is integrable on $\mathrm{range}\,N$ for $\nu_{Z,K}$, and then $\int_{\Theta} g(Nz)\,d\nu_{Z,L} = \kappa \int_{\mathrm{range}\,N} g\,d\nu_{Z,K}$.
--
--   Test functions and matching. $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ and $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathbb{C}$ are continuous with compact support. Transport along the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (commutativity of the tensor product followed by [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57)) turns $\varphi$ into a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ and pushes `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ forward along the inverse isomorphism. The hypothesis `hOn` asserts [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingOn`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L324) for these data with $\sigma^{-1}$, the measure $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, the transported $\varphi$ and $f$: first, whenever $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ has regular semisimple $\sigma^{-1}$-norm string, $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ is regular semisimple, $y$ is a norm conjugator ($\gamma$, pushed into $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, equals $y^{-1}$ times the norm string of $\delta$ times $y$), and Haar measures on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and on the twisted centraliser of $\delta$ are coupled through $y$, then every twisted orbital integral of the transported $\varphi$ over $\delta$ equals every orbital integral of $f$ over $\gamma$; second, for regular semisimple $\gamma$ that is the norm of no $\delta$, every orbital integral of $f$ over $\gamma$ for every Haar measure on the centraliser vanishes.
--
--   Vanishing hypothesis `hvan`. For every $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ in the elliptic cell, every $a \in K^{\times}$ and every $u \in (\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$: if the conjugacy class of $a\gamma_0$ is not in the range of $\mathrm{normClassMap}_{hgen}$, and if there is $c \in (L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-norm string as a scalar matrix equals the image of the scalar matrix of $u$, then for every Haar measure $\tau$ on the centraliser of the single element $\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0) \cdot \mathrm{centralScalar}(a u)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, every complex number $I$ which is an orbital integral of $f$ over that element with respect to $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar` and $\tau$ is zero.
--
--   Per-class transfer hypothesis `hper`. For every $\delta_0 \in R_L$, every $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ in the elliptic cell and every $a \in K^{\times}$ such that the norm class of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted class of $\delta_0$ equals the conjugacy class of $a\gamma_0$,
--   $$\int_{\Theta} \xi_L(z) \Big(\int_{\Psi_L(\delta_0)} \varphi\big(x^{-1}\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\delta_0)\,\mathrm{sigmaAdelicAct}(\mathrm{centralScalar}(z)\,x)\big)\Big)\,d\nu_{Z,L} = \frac{c_0 \kappa}{\ell \cdot \max(1,|\Xi|)} \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \int_{\mathrm{range}\,N} \xi_K(a u) \Big(\int_{\Psi_K(\gamma_0)} f\big(x^{-1}\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0)\,(\mathrm{centralScalar}(a u)\,x)\big)\Big)\,d\nu_{Z,K},$$
--   the inner integrals being taken against `adelicGLHaar`, and $a$ being viewed in $(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$ through the principal-idele embedding.
--
--   Conclusion. Write, for $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$,
--   $$w_L(\delta_0) := \#\Big\{q \in L^{\times}/\{\sigma^{-1}(v)v^{-1} : v \in L^{\times}\} : \exists u \in L^{\times},\ [u] = q \text{ and } \exists h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L),\ u\,\delta_0 = h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(h)\Big\},$$
--   $$J_L(\delta_0) := \int_{\Theta} \xi_L(z) \Big(\int_{\Psi_L(\delta_0)} \varphi\big(x^{-1}\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\delta_0)\,\mathrm{sigmaAdelicAct}(\mathrm{centralScalar}(z)\,x)\big)\Big)\,d\nu_{Z,L},$$
--   and, for $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ and $\xi_K \in \Xi$,
--   $$w_K(\gamma_0) := \#\{a \in K^{\times} : \exists h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K),\ a\gamma_0 = h^{-1}\gamma_0 h\}, \qquad J_K(\xi_K,\gamma_0) := \int_{(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}} \xi_K(z) \Big(\int_{\Psi_K(\gamma_0)} f\big(x^{-1}\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0)\,(\mathrm{centralScalar}(z)\,x)\big)\Big)\,d\nu_{Z,K},$$
--   the cardinalities being `Nat.card` values regarded as complex numbers and inverted (so the weight factor is $0$ when the cardinality is not finite and positive), and the integral defining $J_K$ being over all of $(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$, not over $\mathrm{range}\,N$. Three assertions hold.
--
--   First, the set of those $\delta_0 \in R_L$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted norm class is the conjugacy class of some elliptic $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ and for which $w_L(\delta_0)^{-1} J_L(\delta_0) \neq 0$ is finite.
--
--   Second, for every $\xi_K \in \Xi$, the set of those $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ lying in the elliptic cell with $w_K(\gamma_0)^{-1} J_K(\xi_K,\gamma_0) \neq 0$ is finite.
--
--   Third, the finitary sum over $\delta_0$ in $R_L$ with elliptic norm class satisfies
--   $$\sum_{\delta_0} w_L(\delta_0)^{-1} J_L(\delta_0) = \frac{c_0 \kappa}{\ell \cdot \max(1,|\Xi|)} \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi}\ \sum_{\gamma_0 \in R_K \cap \mathrm{elliptic}} w_K(\gamma_0)^{-1} J_K(\xi_K,\gamma_0),$$
--   the coefficient being the real number $c_0 \kappa / (\ell \cdot \max(1,|\Xi|))$ viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, and the sums over $\delta_0$ and $\gamma_0$ being finitary sums over the indicated sets, legitimate by the first two assertions.
--
--   This is the assembly step of the elliptic part in the comparison of a twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension $L/K$ of prime degree with the ordinary trace formula over $K$: the weighted sum over twisted classes with elliptic norm class is identified, term by term via the per-class transfer identity and then globally, with the corresponding weighted sum of elliptic class integrals over $K$ summed over the characters in $\Xi$. It feeds the version of the same identity in which the per-class identity is replaced by the matching and vanishing hypotheses, on the route to cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}_2$.
